        <obo:IAO_0000115>Joint fluid is a transudate of plasma that is actively secreted by synovial cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Portion of organism substance that is a clear fluid that occupies the space in synovial joints.[TAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000009>It provides nutrients and lubrication for articular cartilage</obo:UBPROP_0000009>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000010>The fluid contains hyaluronan secreted by fibroblast-like cells in the synovial membrane, lubricin (proteoglycan 4; PRG4) secreted by the surface chondrocytes of the articular cartilage and interstitial fluid filtered from the blood plasma</obo:UBPROP_0000010>
